Time zones for daytime(2), in Inferno's format: a line with the
standard time's name and offset east of Greenwich in seconds, and the
daylight time's, then the start and end of each period of daylight time
from 1970 to 2037, in seconds since 1970 as counted on standard time.

timezone is the zone programs use. It is GMT; to change it, copy or
bind another file over it, or set $timezone to a zone's text or to the
name of its file.

The files are made from the IANA time zone database, which is in the
public domain, by `cargo xtask timezones`; see tzdata/README in the
source tree.
